13. Tibetan gorshey adaptation. Keep the same rig:
- a roughly 6:5 rounded-rect patch of dry highland grass with the dithered edge;
- a ring of 6-10 dancers (block bodies about 24 art-px tall) in chuba robes with long sleeves (thin boxes that swing);
- a small central fire or offering pile, a stone or whitewashed house corner, and lungta prayer-flag lines (thin Lines with small coloured quads that sway 1px);
- animation: the ring rotates slowly while each dancer does a sleeve swing and step on beats, all at integer frequencies within one loop of about 8-12 s.
